  "notes": {
    "teams.social": "Official channels, linked from each team's squad page. Franchises do rename their handles after a rebrand (RCB did in 2024), so these are worth a look whenever a team changes its name.",
    "teams.info": "Key order here is the team order calibrate_match_model() fits its ratings in, and the order the /teams squad make-up counts are built in. Keep all ten franchises listed.",
    "teams.ids": "Feed team id -> [abbreviation, full name]. Written as strings because JSON object keys always are; config.py casts them back to int for team_abbr(). The two TBA ids are the placeholder sides the feed uses for unresolved playoff fixtures.",
    "colors.match": "Brand triple per team. CSK c2 has also been run as #fdcd05 and #f15c19.",
    "colors.squad": "Squad-page gradient pairs, c1 -> c2: CSK yellow to navy blue, MI blue to gold, RCB red to black, KKR purple to gold, SRH orange to black, DC blue to red, PBKS red to gold, RR pink to blue, GT navy to gold, LSG light blue to gold.",
    "urls.stats": "Alternative feed that has been used before, currently unused: https://www.cricbuzz.com/api/cricket-series/series-stats/9241/",
    "stats_list": "Key order sets the order the leaderboards are seeded into Toppers, and so the order they appear on the stats pages."
